    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "L1 chunk rates: writes, evictions, peer fetches",
      "description": "All four series are chunks/s, so they share an axis honestly. The question this panel exists to answer: does 'evicted/s, counter' track 'peer fetches/s'? On 2026-08-17 l1_evicted_chunks_total was 2,639 and l2_prefetch_load_submitted was 2,639, exactly, while chunk_idle_before_evict_seconds_count was 6. If those two rates move together, chunks fetched from the peer are not retained locally and every cross-node hit is re-fetched. Resident chunk count lives in the 'L1 memory in use' panel, which is the same data unscaled. Note: LRU evictions/s comes from a histogram LMCache creates lazily on the first eviction. Before L1 first reaches the watermark the metric does not exist and the series reads no data, which is not the same as reading zero.",
